{"p4": {"friction": "The rubric doesn't say how to treat an intro theorem cross-labelled to a later result, \"Theorem 1.1 (Corollary 5.2)\": it could be equivalent-to between results, or no relation at all. Proposition 4.7 uses the word \"defines\" (\"this construction defines a contravariant functor Spec\") for a symbol already introduced in Definition 4.4.", "doubt": "Claim 6: whether a cross-label counts as an equivalence of results when the hypotheses differ (affine vs FSch^qt). Claim 5: whether giving a functor its action on morphisms counts as introducing a term.", "missing_context": "The paper text has no proofs or section bodies, only statements, so depends-on or technique claims couldn't have been checked. None were present here.", "proposed_change": "Add to the equivalent-to boundary: a restatement cross-label such as 'Theorem 1.1 (Corollary 5.2)' is equivalent-to (sense: iff) only if both statements match in their hypotheses; otherwise grade wrong-relation.", "process_observation": "Claims 9/18 and 2/10 are near-duplicates. The extractor emitted the same assertion twice with different subject strings."}}
